.SH NAME
line \- read one line from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B line
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Line\^
copies one line (up to a new-line) from the standard
input and writes it on the standard output.
It returns an exit code of 1 on
.SM
.B EOF
and always prints at least a new-line. 
It is often used within shell files to
read from the user's terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
gets(1C), sh(1), read(2).
